-----------------------------Basic Linux Commands-----------------------------------------------------
ls- used to list all the files and directories under the current working directory
pwd-used to display the path of current working directory
mkdir- used to create new directories or folders
cd - used to change the current working directory
rmdir - used to delete empty directories.
cat - used to display file contents
cp - used to copy files or directories
mv - used to move or rename files and directories.
rm - used to delete files permanently
uname - 
touch - used to create empty files
locate - used to find files using
clear - used to clear the terminal
whoami - display the current user
df -h - display disk space usage
wc -l → Number of lines
wc -w → Number of words
wc -c → Number of bytes
wc -m → Number of characters

